<!--
  TallyPrime "Stock Summary" report. Structure copied from a live response
  (2026-08-14); every name and figure below is INVENTED, per the no-real-data
  rule enforced by tests/noRealData.test.ts.

  Deliberately not a clean happy path. It carries, in order:

  1. A normal item, whose rate is ROUNDED such that quantity x rate does NOT
     equal the reported value: 400.00 x 2.50 = 1,000.00 but the value is
     -1,004.32. This is the live behaviour and the reason the tool forbids
     recomputing value from rate.
  2. An item whose DSPCLQTY element is EMPTY. Must read as null, never zero.
  3. A row with a name but NO DSPSTKINFO block at all — the shape a heading or
     subtotal row takes. It must still pair correctly and must not consume the
     NEXT row's figures, which is the silent mispairing that positional parsing
     exists to avoid.
  4. An item whose value is not a number. Must become null plus a warning
     rather than a salvaged figure.
  5. A genuine ZERO value, which must survive as 0 and be distinguishable
     from the nulls above.
-->
<ENVELOPE>
 <DSPACCNAME>
  <DSPDISPNAME>Invented Widget 10mm</DSPDISPNAME>
</DSPACCNAME>
 <DSPSTKINFO>
  <DSPSTKCL>
   <DSPCLQTY>400.00 Nos</DSPCLQTY>
   <DSPCLRATE>2.50</DSPCLRATE>
   <DSPCLAMTA>-1004.32</DSPCLAMTA>
</DSPSTKCL>
</DSPSTKINFO>
 <DSPACCNAME>
  <DSPDISPNAME>Invented Gasket</DSPDISPNAME>
</DSPACCNAME>
 <DSPSTKINFO>
  <DSPSTKCL>
   <DSPCLQTY></DSPCLQTY>
   <DSPCLRATE>7.00</DSPCLRATE>
   <DSPCLAMTA>-70.00</DSPCLAMTA>
</DSPSTKCL>
</DSPSTKINFO>
 <DSPACCNAME>
  <DSPDISPNAME>Invented Subtotal Row</DSPDISPNAME>
</DSPACCNAME>
 <DSPACCNAME>
  <DSPDISPNAME>Invented Unreadable Item</DSPDISPNAME>
</DSPACCNAME>
 <DSPSTKINFO>
  <DSPSTKCL>
   <DSPCLQTY>12.00 Kg</DSPCLQTY>
   <DSPCLRATE>1.00</DSPCLRATE>
   <DSPCLAMTA>not a number</DSPCLAMTA>
</DSPSTKCL>
</DSPSTKINFO>
 <DSPACCNAME>
  <DSPDISPNAME>Invented Zero Stock Item</DSPDISPNAME>
</DSPACCNAME>
 <DSPSTKINFO>
  <DSPSTKCL>
   <DSPCLQTY>0.00 Nos</DSPCLQTY>
   <DSPCLRATE>0.00</DSPCLRATE>
   <DSPCLAMTA>0.00</DSPCLAMTA>
</DSPSTKCL>
</DSPSTKINFO>
</ENVELOPE>
